{"name":"Porch Ceiling","hex":"#a4b3b9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"porch","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A covered entrance to a building, whether taken from the interior, and forming a sort of vestibule within the main wall, or projecting without and with a separate roof. A porch often has chair(s), table(s) and swings.","A portico; a covered walk."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/porch"},{"term":"ceiling","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The overhead closure of a room.","The upper limit of an object or action."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of ceil"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ceiling"}],"entries":[{"title":"Porch","blocks":[{"text":"A porch is a room or gallery located in front of an entrance to a building. A porch is placed in front of the façade of a building it commands, and forms a low front. Alternatively, it may be a vestibule or a projecting building that houses the entrance door of a building."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Chartres_Cathedral_020_south_facade_TTaylor.JPG/330px-Chartres_Cathedral_020_south_facade_TTaylor.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Porch"},{"title":"Ceiling","blocks":[{"text":"A ceiling is an overhead interior roof that covers the upper limits of a room. It is not generally considered a structural element, but a finished surface concealing the underside of the roof structure or the floor of a story above. Ceilings can be decorated to taste, and there are many examples of frescoes and artwork on ceilings, especially within religious buildings. A ceiling can also be the upper limit of a tunnel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Ravenna%2C_basilica_di_San_Vitale_%28036%29.jpg/330px-Ravenna%2C_basilica_di_San_Vitale_%28036%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_c